{#-
  The signup form, shared by the issue page and the subscribe page.

  Buttondown's form embed rather than their iframe. Three reasons, all of which
  matter more here than they would on an ordinary site:

  * An iframe fetches a third-party document on every visit, from every reader,
    subscriber or not. This publication switched off open and click tracking
    deliberately; loading someone else's page for everyone would undo that one
    layer out.
  * An iframe cannot be styled. Every colour on this site is stated explicitly
    and the theme is single by choice; theirs arrives with a 1px #ccc border
    matching nothing.
  * Theirs ships fixed at height:220px with scrolling="no", so anything taller
    than that is clipped with no way to reach it.

  Submitting navigates to Buttondown's confirmation page. That is the trade, and
  it is a fair one — their page explains the double opt-in and tells the reader
  to go and confirm, which a "thanks!" in place would not.

  Two changes to the snippet Buttondown generated:
  * `required` on the input, so an empty submit is caught by the browser rather
    than by a round trip to their server.
  * `rel="noopener"` on their referral link. target="_blank" without it leaves
    the opened page able to reach back through window.opener.
-#}
<section class="subscribe" aria-labelledby="subscribe-heading">
  <h2 id="subscribe-heading">Get it in your inbox</h2>
  <p class="pitch">
    One email a {{ brand.CADENCE_NOUN }}, free. Every item links to its source.
  </p>
  <form action="{{ subscribe_action }}" method="post" class="embeddable-buttondown-form">
    {#- A real label, not a placeholder doing its job. A placeholder vanishes on
        focus and is not reliably announced by a screen reader. Visually hidden
        here because the heading above already says it, but present for anyone
        navigating by form controls. -#}
    <label for="bd-email" class="visually-hidden">Your email address</label>
    <div class="row">
      <input id="bd-email" type="email" name="email" required
             autocomplete="email" placeholder="you@example.com"
             aria-describedby="subscribe-note">
      <button type="submit">Subscribe</button>
    </div>
    <p class="note" id="subscribe-note">
      No spam, and unsubscribe in one click.
      <a href="{{ referral_url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Powered by Buttondown</a>.
    </p>
  </form>
</section>
